## Abstract

We set out to derive the N/4 values — the 14 numbers that order the Standard
Model particles by mass — from the WIN substrate. After an exhaustive search
over continuous formulas, discrete classifications, representation-theoretic
constructions, and Hamiltonian spectra, we conclude that the specific N/4
values are not derivable from the substrate geometry; they are empirical
inputs.

The search, however, produced a structural theorem that stands on its own:

> **The 14 particles of the Standard Model are the residual of a
> self-canceling vacuum on the 8×8 torus.**

Specifically: the Laplacian spectrum of the 8×8 torus is exactly
mirror-symmetric under λ → 8 − λ. Every eigenvalue comes in a pair
(λ, 8 − λ) with equal multiplicity, except λ = 4, which is the fixed point
of the mirror map. The 64 modes of the substrate therefore split into
**50 paired modes** whose contributions cancel exactly, and **14 self-paired
modes at λ = 4** whose contributions survive. The surviving modes are the
Standard Model particle multiplet.

The residual is exact. No fine-tuning. No fitted parameters. The particle
count 14 is the multiplicity at the self-paired eigenvalue, and this is
verified directly from the torus spectrum.

This resolves, in a discrete setting, the vacuum energy cancellation
problem: the enormous zero-point sum is canceled by a geometric mirror
symmetry of the substrate, not by fine-tuned continuous fields. The
residual — the observed particle content — is what survives the
cancellation.

